WEBVTT

00:56.688 --> 00:59.013
These are the last two eggs.

01:07.323 --> 01:09.315
From my own bookshelf.

01:09.367 --> 01:12.485
- Help you pass the time.
- I've already read it.

01:12.537 --> 01:15.946
You might catch something
you missed the second time around.

01:18.167 --> 01:21.035
Why did you move me
from the rec room down here?

01:21.129 --> 01:23.621
I wanted you under my own roof.

01:27.301 --> 01:30.221
Where are you keeping
your other prisoner? Miles, is it?

01:31.431 --> 01:34.924
- Or you don't want to share.
- I was hoping you would share, Ben,

01:34.976 --> 01:37.551
seeing as you claimed
to have a spy on his ship.

01:42.775 --> 01:45.976
I feel for you, John. I really do.

01:46.738 --> 01:48.813
You keep hitting dead ends.

01:50.950 --> 01:55.528
You couldn't find the cabin,
you can't make contact with Jacob.

01:55.580 --> 01:59.907
You're so desperate to figure out what
to do next you're asking me for help.

02:03.212 --> 02:06.132
So here we are, just like old times.

02:06.758 --> 02:09.041
Except I'm locked in a different room.

02:12.305 --> 02:15.058
And you're more lost
than you ever were.

02:16.476 --> 02:18.551
I know what you're trying to do.

02:18.644 --> 02:20.104
It's not gonna work.

02:20.146 --> 02:23.764
- Excellent, John. You're evolving.
- Done with your breakfast?

02:46.047 --> 02:47.674
What's that all about?

02:49.467 --> 02:51.459
Who knows? It's Locke.

02:53.346 --> 02:55.254
Mornin', ladies.

02:55.306 --> 02:58.174
- Good morning.
- Mornin'.

02:59.936 --> 03:01.896
Coffee smells good.

03:01.938 --> 03:06.067
Well, why don't I go make you a cup?

03:12.615 --> 03:14.492
Kinda weird, ain't it?

03:15.702 --> 03:19.320
Sitting on porches,
drinking coffee out of mugs.

03:19.372 --> 03:21.822
Anyway, I found some clothes
about your size.

03:21.874 --> 03:23.751
Hung 'em in the closet.

03:23.793 --> 03:27.745
- So after I kick out Hugo...
- I'm not moving in with you, James.

03:29.298 --> 03:34.001
- Well... then why did you stay?
- That's none of your business.

03:34.053 --> 03:36.837
You got a secret agenda, huh?

03:37.765 --> 03:40.716
- If you're spying for Jack...
- I'm not spying for anyone.

03:40.768 --> 03:43.552
- Why don't you tell...?
- Because I don't trust you.

03:47.191 --> 03:49.558
This is about the pregnancy thing.

03:53.614 --> 03:55.898
- James.
- Yeah?

03:56.659 --> 03:57.733
Go home.

04:00.496 --> 04:02.206
OK, fine.

04:05.710 --> 04:07.253
See you later then.

04:19.807 --> 04:21.517
You ready?

04:22.143 --> 04:23.551
Is there a back entrance?

04:23.603 --> 04:25.803
Yeah, but you're going in
the front door

04:25.855 --> 04:27.972
with your head held high, OK?

04:30.318 --> 04:32.726
Yeah. OK.

04:33.946 --> 04:35.354
Let's do this.

04:37.742 --> 04:39.535
Why did you do it, Kate?

04:41.788 --> 04:43.581
What was your statement?

04:46.167 --> 04:50.035
Folks, we're not making any statements
or answering any questions.

04:55.259 --> 04:58.429
<i>The People v. Katherine Anne Austen.</i>

04:58.471 --> 05:01.172
The Honourable Arthur Galzethron
presiding.

05:01.265 --> 05:04.884
The bailiff will read the counts.
Will the defendant please rise?

05:05.353 --> 05:08.721
Katherine Anne Austen,
you are charged with fraud,

05:08.773 --> 05:11.265
arson, assault on a federal officer,

05:11.317 --> 05:13.277
assault with a deadly weapon,

05:13.319 --> 05:16.072
grand larceny, grand theft auto

05:16.155 --> 05:18.314
and murder in the first degree.

05:18.366 --> 05:20.775
Miss Austen, how do you plead?

05:24.247 --> 05:25.821
Not guilty.

05:26.374 --> 05:28.866
Thus entered.
I'll now hear argument on bail.

05:30.294 --> 05:33.297
Your Honour, we are requesting
the defendant be remanded

05:33.339 --> 05:35.623
into custody
for the duration of the trial.

05:35.675 --> 05:38.292
My client's been free
pending arraignment.

05:38.344 --> 05:41.462
- Now she's a flight risk?
- The definition of a flight risk.

05:41.514 --> 05:45.727
She has one of the most recognisable
faces. Where will she run?

05:45.768 --> 05:48.302
Miss Austen,
based on your prior history,

05:48.354 --> 05:50.471
I'm inclined to agree with the People.

05:50.565 --> 05:54.308
You're remanded into federal custody
for the duration of your trial.

05:54.360 --> 05:56.727
Bailiff, take the defendant
into custody.

05:57.864 --> 05:59.688
Sorry.

06:25.725 --> 06:28.050
"Albuquerque"?

06:28.144 --> 06:30.136
Too hot.

06:31.773 --> 06:33.931
- New York.
- Too many people.

06:44.452 --> 06:47.737
I learn English for you.

06:49.999 --> 06:57.455
To live in America.

07:05.390 --> 07:07.423
Hey, look! Jack!

07:09.227 --> 07:10.853
Jack!

07:13.439 --> 07:14.513
Hey, man.

07:14.565 --> 07:17.902
This is... Charlotte, Dan.

07:19.404 --> 07:23.647
Their helicopter already took Sayid
and Desmond back to their freighter.

07:23.700 --> 07:27.067
They can make arrangements
to get all of us off this island.

07:27.412 --> 07:28.871
Where's Kate?

07:31.749 --> 07:33.376
She stayed with Locke.

07:38.506 --> 07:39.580
Hello, Kate.

07:41.217 --> 07:42.927
Is that blood?

07:42.969 --> 07:45.669
I just killed a chicken.

07:46.639 --> 07:48.266
What can I do for you?

07:48.933 --> 07:51.717
I want to talk to Miles.
Where are you keeping him?

07:51.769 --> 07:54.970
- Why do you need to talk to him?
- That's personal.

07:56.107 --> 07:58.015
No.

07:58.067 --> 08:01.769
- And what gives you the right...
- You may think this is a democracy

08:01.821 --> 08:05.158
because of the way Jack ran things.
This is not a democracy.

08:07.410 --> 08:10.027
Then I guess that makes it
a dictatorship.

08:10.580 --> 08:14.407
If I was a dictator, I would just
shoot you and go about my day.

08:16.044 --> 08:18.327
Dinner's at 6.00 if you're hungry.

08:26.554 --> 08:28.014
Hey, Hurley.

08:28.056 --> 08:30.673
Wait. You bringing that to Miles?

08:30.725 --> 08:32.758
- Yeah.
- Locke asked me to do it.

08:32.810 --> 08:35.094
Cool. That dude creeps me out.

08:35.146 --> 08:38.806
- He's still in the rec room, right?
- I moved him to the boathouse...

08:44.781 --> 08:47.314
You just totally
Scooby-Doo'd me, didn't you?

08:47.367 --> 08:48.482
Sorry.

08:49.035 --> 08:52.205
- You're not gonna let him go, are you?
- No. No, I promise.

08:52.246 --> 08:54.321
Just don't tell Locke it was me.

09:28.074 --> 09:30.316
So the Arab traded you too.

09:40.211 --> 09:43.297
- Do you know who I am?
- Excuse me?

09:43.339 --> 09:45.498
Do you know who I am?

09:47.677 --> 09:49.387
Do you know what I did?

09:51.431 --> 09:53.391
What did you do?

09:54.183 --> 09:55.810
Answer the question.

09:59.439 --> 10:00.513
OK.

10:02.859 --> 10:04.819
I'll tell you what you want to know,

10:04.861 --> 10:06.977
but you gotta do something
for me first.

10:08.114 --> 10:11.065
- I'm not letting you go.
- I don't want to be let go.

10:11.117 --> 10:12.942
I am exactly where I want to be.

10:15.330 --> 10:20.699
What I want is one minute
of someone's time.

10:21.627 --> 10:23.536
You bring him to me...

10:23.588 --> 10:27.633
...and I will tell you
everything I know about you.

10:29.010 --> 10:30.251
Who?

10:34.098 --> 10:35.808
Who do you think?

10:51.157 --> 10:53.910
- Are you OK?
- Yeah, fine.

10:54.661 --> 10:58.404
Listen, the DA's decided
to try this case herself...

10:59.207 --> 11:02.126
...which means they're
gonna do the full-court press.

11:02.168 --> 11:04.577
We need to start talking about
cutting a deal.

11:04.629 --> 11:06.589
- What kind of deal?
- My best guess,

11:06.631 --> 11:09.749
I'd say she'll take a 15-year sentence.

11:09.801 --> 11:12.804
- And you serve seven.
- No way.

11:14.597 --> 11:17.684
If you go to trial, you're looking
at 20 years on each count

11:17.725 --> 11:19.884
and a life sentence
on the murder charge.

11:19.936 --> 11:22.553
- No.
- Kate, you confessed to your mother

11:22.605 --> 11:26.348
that you killed your father,
and now she's their star witness.

11:27.443 --> 11:30.446
What am I supposed to do?
How am I supposed to win this?

11:30.530 --> 11:32.073
Put me on the stand.

11:32.156 --> 11:34.857
And take a chance with the DA
crossing you? No.

11:35.618 --> 11:38.569
Way I see it,
we've got one shot at this.

11:38.621 --> 11:41.290
- What's that?
- We make it about character.

11:41.374 --> 11:44.711
Not about what you did or didn't do,
but about who you are.

11:46.087 --> 11:48.245
What do you mean, who I am?

11:49.757 --> 11:52.875
- I want him in the courtroom.
- Absolutely not.

11:52.927 --> 11:55.419
We need him, Kate.
It'll generate sympathy.

11:55.471 --> 11:58.589
Duncan, listen to me.
You are not bringing him in here.

11:58.641 --> 12:01.728
You want to make this about me,
my character, fine.

12:01.769 --> 12:05.815
But you are not using my son.

12:11.529 --> 12:14.230
Maybe we should try a number
other than the boat,

12:14.282 --> 12:16.107
like 911.

12:19.912 --> 12:21.570
What's wrong?

12:21.622 --> 12:25.324
Nothing. We're just having trouble
getting a hold of their boat.

12:25.376 --> 12:29.286
You haven't heard from Sayid?
You said they left yesterday.

12:29.339 --> 12:31.080
And I'm sure they're fine.

12:33.384 --> 12:34.761
What if Locke was right?

12:34.802 --> 12:37.002
What if these people
are here to hurt us?

12:37.096 --> 12:39.130
Locke has no idea what he's doing.

12:39.974 --> 12:41.632
Then why is Kate with him?

12:52.654 --> 12:55.438
You sure he's got Ben
in his basement?

12:55.490 --> 12:58.065
I saw Rousseau take him
in there last night.

12:58.117 --> 13:01.694
- And does Locke ever go out?
- He's been in there cooking all day.

13:01.746 --> 13:03.988
He invited us all over for dinner.

13:06.167 --> 13:08.075
Can you get Aaron for me?

13:11.089 --> 13:13.622
Just pick him up
and rock him a little bit.

13:17.011 --> 13:20.296
Yeah, I'm just...
not very good with babies.

13:20.348 --> 13:22.381
I wouldn't want him
to get more upset.

13:24.477 --> 13:26.135
Here, I got him.

13:31.609 --> 13:33.017
It's OK.

13:33.111 --> 13:35.071
There we go, muffin.

13:36.322 --> 13:37.396
There we go.

13:38.908 --> 13:40.900
You're so good with him.

13:43.162 --> 13:44.236
What?

13:44.288 --> 13:48.115
Just the last thing I ever thought
I'd be good at is being a mom.

13:49.627 --> 13:52.161
You know, you should try it sometime.

13:52.213 --> 13:54.538
Hey, Aaron.

13:58.886 --> 14:00.294
Please rise.

14:03.725 --> 14:06.394
Court is now in session.
Please be seated.

14:12.942 --> 14:15.434
- Don't fire me, OK?
- What?

14:15.486 --> 14:18.687
We got killed in the opening.
I had to do this.

14:18.740 --> 14:20.898
Does the defence have a witness?

14:22.285 --> 14:23.776
Yes, we do, Your Honour.

14:23.828 --> 14:27.655
The defence calls Dr Jack Shephard
to the witness stand.

14:37.508 --> 14:40.543
Your Honour, I'd like to renew
my objection to this witness

14:40.636 --> 14:44.766
- on the basis of relevance.
- And I'll renew my overruling.

14:45.350 --> 14:48.519
You have to be aware this witness
did not meet the defendant

14:48.561 --> 14:51.762
until after the alleged crimes
she's being charged with.

14:51.814 --> 14:54.849
He is to be viewed
as a character witness only.

14:55.818 --> 14:58.144
- Proceed.
- Please raise your right hand.

14:58.196 --> 15:00.604
Do you swear to tell the truth,
the whole truth

15:00.657 --> 15:02.940
and nothing but the truth,
so help you God?

15:02.992 --> 15:04.400
Yes.

15:08.873 --> 15:10.197
Dr Shephard.

15:11.834 --> 15:15.004
Could you please tell the ladies
and gentlemen of the jury,

15:15.046 --> 15:18.956
if there are any of you who don't read
newspapers, the internet or watch TV,

15:19.008 --> 15:21.000
how you met the defendant?

15:22.970 --> 15:25.807
On September 22, 2004,

15:25.848 --> 15:28.090
Kate...

15:28.935 --> 15:30.593
Miss Austen and I

15:30.645 --> 15:32.970
were both passengers
on Oceanic flight 815,

15:33.022 --> 15:35.858
which crash-landed on an island
in the South Pacific.

15:35.900 --> 15:38.476
Were you aware Miss Austen
was a fugitive

15:38.528 --> 15:42.688
being transported by a United States
marshal on that flight to Los Angeles?

15:42.740 --> 15:46.233
- I did learn that eventually, yes.
- From the US marshal?

15:46.285 --> 15:48.778
No, the marshal died in the crash.

15:50.540 --> 15:52.114
I never spoke to him.

15:52.166 --> 15:53.991
Miss Austen told me.

15:57.880 --> 16:00.289
Did you ever ask her if she was guilty?

16:00.383 --> 16:02.208
No. Never.

16:02.260 --> 16:05.096
That seems like a reasonable question.
Why not?

16:05.888 --> 16:08.808
I just assumed there had been
some kind of mistake.

16:08.850 --> 16:10.883
And why would you think that?

16:12.854 --> 16:16.347
Only eight of us survived the crash.
We landed in the water.

16:17.400 --> 16:19.517
I was hurt pretty badly.

16:19.569 --> 16:23.562
In fact, if it weren't for her I would
have never made it to the shore.

16:24.532 --> 16:26.857
She took care of me,
took care of all of us.

16:26.909 --> 16:30.194
She gave us first aid, water,

16:30.246 --> 16:32.655
found food, made shelter.

16:32.707 --> 16:35.991
- She tried to save the other two...
- Stop.

16:37.253 --> 16:38.994
Miss Austen, please sit down.

16:39.047 --> 16:42.456
This has nothing to do with...
with anything.

16:45.470 --> 16:48.671
This is my trial, and I don't want him
to say anything else.

16:48.723 --> 16:50.923
That's fine. I have no more questions.

16:53.102 --> 16:55.772
Miss Dunbrook, your witness.

17:00.234 --> 17:02.601
That was very moving, Dr Shephard.

17:03.404 --> 17:06.074
I only have one question for you.

17:06.741 --> 17:09.442
- Do you love the defendant?
- Objection!

17:10.036 --> 17:13.821
You opened this door, Mr Forrester.
I'm going to allow it.

17:16.084 --> 17:17.658
Dr Shephard?

17:19.253 --> 17:21.047
Do you love Miss Austen?

17:23.466 --> 17:24.540
No.

17:26.803 --> 17:28.794
Not anymore.

17:37.772 --> 17:42.016
So, what do you want to watch,
<i>Xanadu</i> or <i>Satan's Doom?</i>

17:42.068 --> 17:43.642
I'm reading.

17:47.031 --> 17:49.565
- Will you turn that thing down?
- Sorry.

17:59.919 --> 18:01.118
Hey.

18:01.212 --> 18:02.588
Can I come in?

18:04.799 --> 18:07.249
Sure. I believe you know my roommate.

18:07.343 --> 18:09.460
- Hi, Hurley.
- Hey, Kate.

18:11.389 --> 18:13.756
You got something in your eye, Hugo?

18:15.018 --> 18:17.051
Why don't we talk in the kitchen.

18:23.901 --> 18:27.728
I know it's in a box,
but it's pretty damn good wine.

18:28.364 --> 18:29.741
I tested it.

18:29.782 --> 18:32.900
So how's life at <i>casa de</i> Claire?

18:32.952 --> 18:37.613
- Baby Aaron keeping you up all night?
- No. He's a good sleeper.

18:37.665 --> 18:39.698
Good for you.

18:46.799 --> 18:48.676
You are terrible at this, Freckles.

18:50.011 --> 18:51.085
Terrible at what?

18:51.179 --> 18:53.796
You already said you didn't
stay behind for me.

18:54.474 --> 18:58.551
At least be woman enough to tell me
you want to use me for something.

19:02.315 --> 19:04.348
I want to use you for something.

19:05.068 --> 19:06.725
See? Wasn't that hard.

19:08.196 --> 19:09.572
For what?

19:09.614 --> 19:11.188
For Ben.

19:13.326 --> 19:16.412
I want you to help me bust him out.

19:21.876 --> 19:23.617
Want to play some backgammon?

19:24.045 --> 19:25.119
You're on.

19:34.889 --> 19:36.922
Do you think I know what I'm doing?

19:39.602 --> 19:43.095
Do you regret following me out here?

19:43.147 --> 19:46.234
Are you worried about
what we should do next?

19:48.569 --> 19:52.438
All I know is I'd be a lot more worried
if I was sitting on that beach.

19:52.490 --> 19:55.024
And the rest of the group,
what are they saying?

19:55.076 --> 19:56.953
I think they're saying "baa".

19:58.037 --> 20:01.322
That's the nice thing about sheep.
They're predictable.

20:05.962 --> 20:07.870
But I ain't so sure about Kate.

20:09.132 --> 20:10.842
What do you mean?

20:12.760 --> 20:15.680
I need your word you ain't gonna
do nothing to her.

20:15.722 --> 20:19.090
- Why would I do anything...?
- Just give me your word, John.

20:22.562 --> 20:25.846
- You know what? Forget it.
- No, no, no. All right.

20:25.898 --> 20:28.265
You have my word.

20:30.361 --> 20:32.478
She came to me about an hour ago.

20:33.239 --> 20:36.409
Said she wanted my help
busting Ben out of your basement.

20:38.077 --> 20:39.819
Why?

20:39.871 --> 20:42.790
She talked to that guy...

20:42.874 --> 20:45.877
Bruce Lee, from the freighter,
the guy you got locked up.

20:45.918 --> 20:48.285
He told her to bring Ben down
to him for a chat.

20:48.338 --> 20:51.539
No, that's impossible.
She doesn't know where Miles is.

20:51.591 --> 20:54.166
The boathouse down by the dock?

20:54.218 --> 20:56.627
If Hugo knows, everybody knows.

21:00.016 --> 21:02.425
- Are you sure about this?
- Yeah, I'm sure.

21:07.190 --> 21:08.816
Where are you going with that?

21:08.858 --> 21:11.475
Whatever Miles has to say to Ben...

21:11.569 --> 21:13.310
...he can say to me.

21:30.963 --> 21:32.997
Son of a bitch.

21:49.565 --> 21:50.942
Come on.

22:18.177 --> 22:20.294
You got one minute. Go.

22:22.682 --> 22:25.716
- How about some privacy?
- Fifty-five seconds.

22:28.521 --> 22:31.555
- You know who I am?
- Yes.

22:33.026 --> 22:35.643
- You know who I work for?
- Yes.

22:35.737 --> 22:39.313
And you know he's put a lot of time
and energy into finding you.

22:42.243 --> 22:44.068
So now I found you.

22:44.162 --> 22:46.570
And I can tell him exactly
where you are.

22:49.208 --> 22:52.785
Or I can lie and tell him
you're already dead.

22:54.255 --> 22:58.551
And I'd be willing to do that
for $3.2 million.

23:01.596 --> 23:04.630
You've arranged this meeting
so you could blackmail me?

23:05.141 --> 23:07.675
It's extortion,
if you want to get technical.

23:07.727 --> 23:10.678
Three-point-two...
Why not 3.3 or 3.4?

23:15.610 --> 23:18.561
What makes you think I have
access to that kind of money?

23:18.613 --> 23:20.688
Do not treat me like I'm one of them,

23:20.740 --> 23:24.483
like I don't know who you are
and what you can do.

23:25.787 --> 23:28.654
Your friend Charlotte has seen me.
She knows I'm alive.

23:28.706 --> 23:32.158
I'll take care of Charlotte. You worry
about getting me the money.

23:32.251 --> 23:33.534
You have two days.

23:33.586 --> 23:37.538
My present situation is a little bit
restricted. Can that be amended?

23:37.590 --> 23:38.706
OK.

23:40.218 --> 23:42.887
- One week, in cash...
- Time's up.

23:42.929 --> 23:45.546
- Don't even think about...
- I said time's up!

23:49.018 --> 23:50.342
This is hot.

23:50.436 --> 23:52.428
You got your meeting.
I want my answer.

23:55.858 --> 23:58.559
We got your name
when you called the freighter.

23:59.112 --> 24:02.229
Of course we know about you
and everybody else on the 815.

24:02.281 --> 24:05.941
- Prove it.
- Your name is Katherine Anne Austen.

24:05.994 --> 24:08.486
You're wanted for murder,
fraud, arson,

24:08.538 --> 24:11.030
whole bunch of other stuff
I can't remember.

24:11.082 --> 24:12.740
You're a fugitive.

24:12.792 --> 24:16.410
You were caught in Australia
and the feds were bringing you back.

24:18.089 --> 24:19.747
So yeah, we know.

24:22.010 --> 24:24.846
If I were you, I'd stay right here
on the island.

24:26.139 --> 24:28.808
Who knows? Maybe you
didn't survive the crash.

24:28.850 --> 24:30.727
Come on, come on.

24:39.318 --> 24:40.945
Go back to your house, Kate.

24:41.696 --> 24:45.648
- John, this has nothing to do with you.
- Go back to your house, Kate!

25:07.013 --> 25:09.797
Hi. You OK?

25:11.601 --> 25:13.259
I couldn't sleep.

25:13.311 --> 25:16.345
Yeah, the beds
take a little getting used to.

25:17.148 --> 25:20.558
- I didn't wake Aaron, did I?
- No. Aaron was born on this island.

25:20.610 --> 25:22.351
He can sleep through anything.

25:23.863 --> 25:25.239
John.

25:27.033 --> 25:31.277
- What are you doing?
- I'd like a moment alone with Kate.

25:31.329 --> 25:33.612
Would you excuse us, please, Claire?

25:35.541 --> 25:37.001
It's OK.

25:41.881 --> 25:45.218
- John...
- I don't need to know why you did

25:45.259 --> 25:47.835
what you did, Kate.

25:47.887 --> 25:50.723
I just need to know what they said
to each other.

25:53.351 --> 25:56.927
Miles told Ben he would lie to
the people he works for on the boat,

25:56.979 --> 26:00.181
tell them Ben was dead for $3.2 million.

26:04.946 --> 26:07.563
Listen, John, I'm sorry.

26:07.615 --> 26:11.192
- I asked you where he was and...
- You're not welcome here anymore.

26:12.537 --> 26:14.737
I want you gone by morning.

26:39.313 --> 26:42.348
I worked it out so you two
can have a few minutes of privacy.

26:42.400 --> 26:45.267
- I don't need any privacy.
- You need to talk to her.

26:47.155 --> 26:48.479
I'll be outside.

26:56.956 --> 26:58.280
Hello, Katherine.

27:01.502 --> 27:03.411
Was it true, what he said?

27:06.174 --> 27:07.967
Dr Shephard.

27:08.009 --> 27:09.583
That you're a hero?

27:19.228 --> 27:20.803
Why won't you talk to me?

27:20.855 --> 27:24.901
Because, Mom, the last time I tried
to talk to you, when you got sick,

27:24.942 --> 27:28.144
when I risked my life to see you,
you called the police.

27:28.196 --> 27:29.520
Please.

27:32.867 --> 27:35.067
I don't want to fight with you,
Katherine.

27:36.579 --> 27:38.696
Why are you here?

27:43.544 --> 27:45.578
Because...

27:47.090 --> 27:48.466
...I...

27:51.886 --> 27:55.629
It all changed,
when I thought you were dead.

28:02.939 --> 28:07.235
My doctors have given me six months
to live for the last four years.

28:08.903 --> 28:11.479
I don't know how long I'm going to last.

28:12.782 --> 28:15.065
I came here to tell you that I...

28:16.411 --> 28:19.163
I don't want to testify against you.

28:28.673 --> 28:30.299
Then don't.

28:35.638 --> 28:37.671
I want to see my grandson.

28:45.231 --> 28:47.306
You came here to make a deal?

28:47.358 --> 28:50.111
Just want to meet him.

28:51.738 --> 28:53.813
I don't want you anywhere near him.

28:58.369 --> 29:00.079
We're finished.

29:01.039 --> 29:02.613
We're finished!

29:07.837 --> 29:08.994
Oh, hey, Freckles.

29:15.762 --> 29:17.420
You OK?

29:22.518 --> 29:25.010
Look, I'm sorry I couldn't do nothing.

29:25.063 --> 29:27.815
I wanted him to think
that you fooled me too.

29:30.360 --> 29:32.643
No sense in him
not trusting both of us.

29:35.406 --> 29:37.283
He wants me gone by tomorrow.

29:38.117 --> 29:40.526
What, he banished you?

29:42.580 --> 29:44.989
Well, I unbanish you.

29:48.586 --> 29:51.339
You can stay right here.

29:52.674 --> 29:54.498
This is my house.

29:59.597 --> 30:01.839
OK, me and Montezuma's house.

30:04.477 --> 30:06.469
You're gonna be all right.

30:07.230 --> 30:08.690
I'll keep you safe.

30:31.963 --> 30:33.788
Time. OK, tell me.

30:33.840 --> 30:35.748
What do you remember?

30:35.800 --> 30:38.834
OK, queen of diamonds?

30:40.596 --> 30:43.547
Then we have the six...

30:43.599 --> 30:46.467
...of clubs. Sorry.

30:47.186 --> 30:50.387
And we have a red ten of...

30:52.900 --> 30:54.360
...hearts, maybe?

31:01.909 --> 31:04.110
It's two out of three.

31:04.871 --> 31:06.153
It's not bad.

31:06.205 --> 31:07.446
It's progress.

31:07.999 --> 31:10.783
Three cards, Charlotte?

31:10.835 --> 31:12.378
Is that progress?

31:12.420 --> 31:13.796
Hey.

31:15.298 --> 31:17.123
I'm calling your boat all day.

31:17.175 --> 31:20.668
- Why isn't anyone answering?
- We're here. How should we know?

31:20.720 --> 31:24.588
- If they're not answering...
- There's only one line on that boat?

31:27.852 --> 31:31.554
There is another number we're only
supposed to use in emergencies.

31:34.567 --> 31:36.308
It's an emergency.

31:44.160 --> 31:45.484
Put it on speaker.

31:57.757 --> 32:00.593
- <i>Yeah?</i>
- Regina, it's Charlotte.

32:00.635 --> 32:05.014
- <i>Why are you calling me on this number?</i>
- Minkowski wasn't answering.

32:05.056 --> 32:09.216
The people on the island want to talk
to their friends, make sure they're OK.

32:09.268 --> 32:10.812
<i>What friends?</i>

32:12.188 --> 32:14.013
They left last night.

32:14.065 --> 32:18.277
- Frank took them up in the helicopter.
- <i>What do you mean they took off?</i>

32:18.319 --> 32:20.603
<i>I thought the helicopter was with you.</i>

32:38.965 --> 32:40.623
Good morning.

32:44.679 --> 32:47.880
Listen, I don't know
what you think you're doing,

32:47.932 --> 32:51.133
- but you're wasting your time.
- Open your mouth.

32:51.185 --> 32:52.510
Open your mouth.

32:52.603 --> 32:54.095
Wide.

32:54.856 --> 32:56.680
Don't talk. Bite down, bite down.

32:58.860 --> 33:01.435
I realise, when I tied you up in here
the other day,

33:01.487 --> 33:04.240
I made the mistake of failing
to introduce myself.

33:04.324 --> 33:05.564
My name is John Locke,

33:05.616 --> 33:08.786
and I'm responsible
for the well-being of this island.

33:08.828 --> 33:11.695
Eventually, Miles, you're gonna
tell me who you are,

33:11.748 --> 33:14.281
and you'll tell me about the people
on the boat

33:14.334 --> 33:16.534
and why you're so interested in Ben.

33:16.586 --> 33:18.160
In the meantime, however,

33:18.212 --> 33:20.621
you're gonna keep your mouth shut.

33:23.718 --> 33:25.511
I learned something yesterday.

33:25.553 --> 33:29.422
No use having rules if there's
no punishment for breaking them.

33:30.183 --> 33:32.716
You'll be fine if you bite down
on the trigger.

33:34.479 --> 33:36.272
Enjoy your breakfast.

34:09.639 --> 34:10.713
Wait, wait.

34:10.765 --> 34:13.048
Wait. Just slow down.

34:13.101 --> 34:16.437
Oh, come on. It's not like
we ain't ever done it before.

34:18.356 --> 34:20.931
I'm cool we didn't go all the way
last night.

34:20.983 --> 34:23.736
I get it. You were sad.

34:23.778 --> 34:26.979
But, I mean, how can you resist

34:27.031 --> 34:30.441
after that whole
"I'll keep you safe" thing?

34:30.493 --> 34:32.401
No. Sawyer.

34:33.579 --> 34:34.904
What?

34:36.124 --> 34:38.032
What'd I say?

34:38.084 --> 34:39.658
Forget it.

34:40.086 --> 34:44.747
Oh, right. You still think
you might be pregnant.

34:46.634 --> 34:48.459
I'm not worried.

34:53.766 --> 34:55.841
And I'm not pregnant.

34:57.562 --> 35:00.648
- Are you sure?
- Yeah, I'm sure.

35:02.734 --> 35:04.110
I mean...

35:05.653 --> 35:08.104
Would it have been
the worst thing in the world?

35:08.156 --> 35:11.159
Yes! It would have been
the worst thing in the world.

35:12.035 --> 35:13.943
What would we have done with a baby?

35:14.954 --> 35:17.822
- I'm going back to the beach.
- The beach?

35:17.874 --> 35:21.242
What, you're leaving?
Because of this? That's that?

35:21.294 --> 35:23.661
You crawl up in my bed one second,
the next...

35:23.713 --> 35:24.787
Goodbye.

35:27.091 --> 35:31.252
Don't make this about me, Kate. You
didn't want a baby any more than I did.

35:31.888 --> 35:35.297
You're looking for some excuse
to split, now you got one.

35:36.893 --> 35:40.386
That's all right, Freckles,
I ain't gonna hold it against you.

35:40.438 --> 35:43.524
I'm just gonna sit right here
in my comfy bed,

35:43.608 --> 35:45.318
because in about a week,

35:45.360 --> 35:49.520
you'll find some reason to get pissed
at Jack and bounce right back to me.

36:15.098 --> 36:18.883
...got back last night, I know
which doctor she's been seeing...

36:19.686 --> 36:21.427
Miss Dunbrook.

36:21.562 --> 36:24.315
Are the People ready to proceed?

36:25.983 --> 36:28.100
May we approach the bench,
Your Honour?

36:28.152 --> 36:29.393
Oh, please.

36:35.660 --> 36:38.329
Unfortunately, Your Honour,
our chief witness,

36:38.413 --> 36:41.781
Diane Jansen, the mother of
the defendant, is unable to testify

36:41.833 --> 36:44.700
- because of medical reasons.
- How long will you need?

36:46.254 --> 36:47.630
I can't say right now.

36:47.672 --> 36:49.830
What I'll do is grant a recess
for lunch,

36:49.882 --> 36:53.334
but be prepared to proceed
with your case after we return.

36:53.428 --> 36:55.961
This court is now in recess.

36:56.014 --> 36:57.557
All rise.

37:00.018 --> 37:01.759
We have to talk.

37:06.315 --> 37:10.142
My key witness spoke to her daughter
yesterday, now she's got cold feet.

37:10.194 --> 37:13.896
Quit posturing. Let's get to it.
What are you offering?

37:15.491 --> 37:16.899
Four years in.

37:20.246 --> 37:23.082
No jail time.
Kate Austen is a worldwide hero

37:23.124 --> 37:26.127
who saved five other people's lives
after a plane crash

37:26.169 --> 37:28.786
and nearly starved to death
on a deserted island.

37:28.838 --> 37:31.372
After all that,
you put this woman on trial

37:31.507 --> 37:34.510
for rescuing her mother
from an abusive husband.

37:34.552 --> 37:38.879
If you think that jury
is gonna give her actual time,

37:38.931 --> 37:42.508
then you must have
a hell of a closing, Melissa.

37:45.730 --> 37:47.106
All right.

37:48.691 --> 37:53.071
Time served plus ten years probation,
agreement she does not leave the state.

37:53.112 --> 37:55.948
- What does that matter? She can...
- I'll take it.

37:56.032 --> 37:59.369
- No, wait, Kate...
- Give me something to sign, I'll sign.

37:59.410 --> 38:02.194
And then I walk out that back door.

38:02.330 --> 38:03.904
I just...

38:06.918 --> 38:08.461
I just want this to be over.

38:10.380 --> 38:12.496
I can do that.

38:12.590 --> 38:15.624
Ten years probation, and you stay put.

38:17.887 --> 38:19.764
I have a child.

38:19.806 --> 38:22.423
I'm not going anywhere.

38:36.948 --> 38:38.272
Hey.

38:42.787 --> 38:44.612
How did you know I'd be here?

38:46.165 --> 38:50.159
Your... lawyer gave me the heads-up.

38:52.255 --> 38:53.454
He owed me one.

38:54.257 --> 38:55.498
Thank you...

38:56.634 --> 38:58.261
...for saying what you did.

38:59.804 --> 39:01.295
You're welcome.

39:02.181 --> 39:05.633
You know, Jack, I've heard you say
that story so many times...

39:05.685 --> 39:08.354
...l'm starting to think you believe it.

39:12.817 --> 39:17.113
I just... I just wanted to tell you
that what I said in there...

39:20.199 --> 39:21.398
...I didn't mean it.

39:29.000 --> 39:32.034
You want to follow me?
Come by for a visit?

39:35.757 --> 39:38.926
I actually have to get over
to the hospital.

39:39.761 --> 39:44.839
But... maybe you and I can grab
some coffee together or something.

39:51.230 --> 39:54.014
I know why you don't
want to see my baby, Jack.

39:56.277 --> 40:00.406
But until you do, until you want to...

40:02.659 --> 40:06.152
...there's no you and me
going for coffee.

40:08.498 --> 40:09.905
But...

40:11.334 --> 40:13.576
...if at any time
you change your mind,

40:13.628 --> 40:16.120
- come and see us.
- Yeah.

40:17.674 --> 40:19.050
OK.

40:29.811 --> 40:31.844
- Bye.
- Bye.

41:16.691 --> 41:18.067
Hello?

41:18.818 --> 41:21.519
Kate. I'm so glad you're back.

41:24.741 --> 41:27.910
- He missed you so much.
- Did you keep him away from the TV?

41:27.952 --> 41:29.329
Absolutely.

41:30.330 --> 41:32.071
I just put him down for a nap.

41:55.605 --> 41:57.263
Hey, buddy.

41:58.316 --> 41:59.390
Hey.

42:06.449 --> 42:07.606
Hey.

42:09.786 --> 42:11.068
Hi, Mommy.

42:15.041 --> 42:16.699
Hi, Aaron.
